    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "unbounded-equation-coverage",
        "severity": "blocking",
        "message": "The Story requires a plotter able to take “any equation” and plot its graph (source line 8), and clarification Q-001, specification generation 2, confirms that broad intent. The specification's REQ-001 and AC-001 say to enter an equation and observe a graph but do not define equation forms or input syntax; its boundary section explicitly says no particular equation syntax is specified. An implementation could pass the current criterion by plotting one chosen equation while rejecting other equation forms, so the broad source obligation is not yet verifiable. Define the required equation forms and syntax, or otherwise specify an observable verification strategy that gives “any equation” a testable boundary."
      }
    ]
